From e8c59c1cc414d08605397421521015c325712476 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: suharvest <suharvest@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 4 Jul 2026 01:35:41 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 38/38] fix(export): carry codec_language_id into the exported
 Talker config at the factory
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The CustomVoice checkpoint stores the language-name -> codec-token map as
codec_language_id, and the C++ runtime (qwen3OmniTTSRuntime.cpp::loadConfig)
reads it from the exported talker/config.json to build the 9-row
language-conditioned prefill. _patch_tts_config — the single choke point
where both the fp16 direct export and the int4 stage2 quantization export
assemble the talker config — carried every codec_* scalar except this map,
so quantized exports shipped without it, the runtime loaded 0 entries, and
CustomVoice language conditioning silently degraded to the 8-row
no-language prefix. The equivalent v0.7.1 fix (1668470) landed in the old
experimental/llm_loader/export_all_cli.py and never reached this branch's
tensorrt_edgellm export chain.

Forward codec_language_id through the existing talker_cfg -> root_config
pick chain (covers both the nested HF layout and the stage2 verbatim root
copy), and add codec_language_id + codec_think_id to
_write_standalone_talker_config so the standalone quant-talker extraction
does not drop them before the downstream patch step. Carry-if-present only:
non-CustomVoice checkpoints get no key injected, and re-patching an
already-correct config is byte-identical, so the fp16 path and other model
types are unaffected.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MHEXK41deYx6375K4q3MQb

diff --git a/tensorrt_edgellm/quantization/qwen3_omni.py b/tensorrt_edgellm/quantization/qwen3_omni.py
index f5e8b7e..1136704 100644
--- a/tensorrt_edgellm/quantization/qwen3_omni.py
+++ b/tensorrt_edgellm/quantization/qwen3_omni.py
@@ -432,10 +432,12 @@ def _write_standalone_talker_config(talker_text_dict: dict, talker_dict: dict,
         "vision_start_token_id",
         "codec_bos_id",
         "codec_eos_token_id",
+        "codec_language_id",
         "codec_nothink_id",
         "codec_pad_id",
         "codec_think_bos_id",
         "codec_think_eos_id",
+        "codec_think_id",
         "num_code_groups",
         "speaker_id",
         "thinker_hidden_size",
diff --git a/tensorrt_edgellm/scripts/export.py b/tensorrt_edgellm/scripts/export.py
index cffd20b..16a72eb 100644
--- a/tensorrt_edgellm/scripts/export.py
+++ b/tensorrt_edgellm/scripts/export.py
@@ -1337,6 +1337,17 @@ def _patch_tts_config(model_dir: str, out_dir: str) -> None:
         if v is not None:
             cfg[key] = v
 
+    # CustomVoice language conditioning map: language name -> codec token id.
+    # The C++ runtime (qwen3OmniTTSRuntime.cpp::loadConfig) reads this dict to
+    # build the 9-row language-conditioned Talker prefill; when the map is
+    # missing it loads 0 entries and silently degrades to the 8-row
+    # no-language prefix. The fp16 direct export and the int4 stage2 export
+    # both assemble the talker config here, so carrying it here fixes both.
+    # Optional for non-CustomVoice models (absent key -> nothing written).
+    lang_map = pick("codec_language_id")
+    if isinstance(lang_map, dict) and lang_map:
+        cfg["codec_language_id"] = lang_map
+
     # tts_model_type (only present in root config, not talker_config).
     if "tts_model_type" in root_config:
         cfg["tts_model_type"] = root_config["tts_model_type"]
